@ Index:   Casio MH-10M desk calculator: 10 digits, COST SELL MAR, TAX+ TAX-, memory, its keypad on the screen
@ Author:  Victor Valdes
@ Version: 0.1.0
@ Source:  https://github.com/valdesvj/mh10m47
@ Tested:  C47 simulator (python/c47sim.py): tests/test_mh10m.py, Casio examples worked by hand and 400 random
@ Tested:  key sequences against a separate Python model of the Casio's rules; every screen against the glyphs
@ Tested:  not yet on a C47 (the KEY? codes of ENTER, x<>y, +/-, <-, the operators and the second row to check)
@ Input:   the Casio's keys on the C47: 0-9 . + - x / as they are, ENTER =, +/- +/-, <- the Casio's >,
@ Input:   F1-F6 COST SELL MAR % TAX- TAX+, the second row MRC M- M+ C AC RATE-SET, x<>y the end
@ Output:  1 / 3 = shows 0.333333333; x 3 = 0.999999999 (as the Casio); 1500 TAX+ at 8 % shows 1'620.,
@ Output:  TAX+ again 120.; 1000 COST 25 MAR shows SELL 1'333.333333; at the end the value in X
@
@ ---- What it is ----
@ MH-10M 47 turns the C47 into a Casio MH-10M, the small desk calculator with cost, selling price, margin and tax
@ keys. Its 10-digit display (7-segment digits, the decimal point, the thousands marks, the indicators) and its
@ keypad are drawn on the screen; each key you press shows the Casio key it stands for, inverted. It calculates the
@ way the Casio does: algebraic entry, left to right with no precedence (2 + 3 x 4 = gives 20), results cut (not
@ rounded) to the 10 digits shown, the constant of =, the Casio's %, a memory, cost / sell / margin and tax.
@
@ ---- How to use it ----
@ Load MH10M and press XEQ MH10M. Then use the C47's keys as the Casio's:
@   0-9 .  + - x /   as they are                 ENTER   =
@   +/-              change sign                 <-      the Casio's > (the last digit keyed off)
@   F1 F2 F3         COST  SELL  MAR             F4 F5 F6   %  TAX-  TAX+
@   the second row (the six keys under the soft keys): MRC  M-  M+  C  AC  RATE SET
@   x<>y             OFF: the end; the value shown is put in X
@ Examples: 1 / 3 = shows 0.333333333 and x 3 = then 0.999999999, as on the Casio. 1500 + 15 % gives 1725.
@ COST, SELL and MAR (the margin on the selling price): key two of them, the third is worked out: 1000 COST 25 MAR
@ shows the selling price 1333.333333. Tax: set the rate with RATE SET, the rate, RATE SET; then 1500 TAX+ at 8 %
@ gives 1620 and TAX+ again shows the tax itself (120); TAX- takes the tax out. MRC recalls the memory, MRC twice
@ clears it; M+ and M- finish the calculation first. E (an overflow or a division by 0): only C (go on with the
@ value) and AC work. C clears the number being keyed; AC clears everything but the memory and the tax rate.
@
@ ---- What it changes on your calculator ----
@ Your stack and LASTx are given back at the end, with the value shown pushed into X (as after a calculation).
@ Registers R00-R19 are not touched; R20-R91 are used and cleared at the end. The memory and the tax rate are kept
@ between runs in two variables, MHMEM and MHTAX (delete them to forget them). The screen is cleared at the end;
@ GRMOD 0 and GRFNT 20 are set; WSIZE is set to 64.
@
@ ---- Programs and labels ----
@ One program, MH10M, with one global label (MH10M). Every routine inside is a local label (LBL 00-10 the digit
@ glyphs, 11-85 the keys by their KEY? codes, called with XEQ IND, 86-96 the operations), so nothing else is added
@ to your program catalogue. It uses the STRUCT commands (IF / ELSE / ENDIF, DO / WHILE / ENDDO), ATEXT, GRFNT and
@ AGRAPH of the C47 / R47 firmware. Some KEY? codes (ENTER, x<>y, +/-, <-, the operators, the second row) are not
@ yet confirmed on a calculator: see the README.
@
@ ---- Technical notes (from the commented source) ----
@ MH10M v0.1.0 - MH-10M 47: the Casio MH-10M desk calculator on the C47 / R47
@ The 10-digit LCD (7-segment digits drawn with AGRAPH, the decimal point and the thousands marks) and
@ the Casio's keypad drawn on the screen: the key pressed is shown inverted (XOR) until the next key.
@ It works as the Casio: algebraic entry (no stack), left to right; 10 digits, the results truncated to
@ what the display shows (as the Casio keeps them: 1 / 3 x 3 = 0.999999999); the constant of = (K: for
@ x the first number, for + - / the second); % (a x b % = ab/100, a / b % = 100a/b, a + b % = a + ab/100,
@ a - b % = a - ab/100); MRC (once: recall, twice: clear), M+ and M- (they finish the calculation first);
@ COST, SELL, MAR (margin on the selling price: two give the third); TAX+ and TAX- with the tax rate
@ (pressed twice: the tax amount); RATE SET; E: overflow (the display shows the result / 10^10) or
@ division by 0, only C or AC go on.
@ C47 keys: the digits, . and + - x / as they are; ENTER =; +/- +/-; <- (backspace) the Casio's >;
@ F1-F6 the Casio's top row COST SELL MAR % TAX- TAX+; the second row of the C47 (under the soft keys)
@ MRC M- M+ C AC RATE-SET; x<>y OFF (the end).
@ The tax rate and the memory are kept between runs in the global variables MHTAX and MHMEM
@ (0 STO+ makes them when they are not there).
@ Screen 400 x 240, row 0 = bottom. ATEXT in GRFNT 21 (the title in GRFNT 10). GRMOD and GRFNT take X.
@ The user's stack and LASTx are kept (LocR 10: STOS R.00, LASTx in R.08); at the end the display's
@ value is put in X (the stack lifted, as a calculation) and R20-R91 are cleared (R-CLR 20.72).
@ Registers: R20 X (the value shown), R21 the first number (ACC), R22 the operation pending (86 + 87 -
@ 88 x 89 /, 0 none), R23 the constant's operation, R24 the constant K, R25 1 while a number is keyed,
@ R26 the digits keyed (an integer N), R27 their number, R28 the decimals keyed (-1 no point yet),
@ R29 1 negative, R30 E (error), R31 the memory, R32 the tax rate, R33 the key, R34 the key before,
@ R35 the indicators of the key (COST ... RATE), R36 the indicators shown, R37 the tax amount, R38 1 in
@ RATE SET, R39 COST R40 SELL R41 MAR, R42 the first of two cost/sell/margin keyed (1-3, 0 none),
@ R43 1 when a number was given since the last operation (keyed or MRC), R44 10^decimals keyed,
@ R45 the display's digits (N), R46 its decimals, R47 q, R48 the cell k (0 the right), R49 the cells
@ with a digit (from the right), R50-R59 the digit
@ shown in each cell (10 blank), R60-R69 the mark shown after each cell (1 point, 2 thousands),
@ R70-R72 the glyph's words (left, middle, right columns), R73 a counter, R74 work, R75-R78 work,
@ R79 10^10, R80 the point's word, R81 the thousands mark's word, R84 the AGRAPH word of LBL :RUN:,
@ R85 the keys used ("/11/12/.../"), R86 the value of R45 and R46, R87-R89 the key shown inverted (x, row, height 1 or 2 key rows;
@ 0 none), R90 23 ones, R91 52 ones (the inside of a key).
@ Indicators (R35, R36): 1 M, 2 minus, 4 E, 8 COST, 16 SELL, 32 MAR, 64 TAX+, 128 TAX-, 256 TAX,
@ 512 SET, 1024 RATE.
@ The digits: cell k (0-9, from the right) at x 331 - 31k, 24 columns (4 left, 16 middle, 4 right),
@ the mark after it at x 356 - 31k (4 columns); AGRAPH words from row 145 (64 rows, GRMOD 1: written
@ as they are), segments 48 rows high from row 151.
@ The keypad: key (c, r) (c 0-5 from the left, r 0-4 from the bottom) at x 3 + 66c, row 1 + 29r,
@ 62 x 25 (the + key 62 x 54, rows 0 and 1).
@ Labels: LBL 00-10 the glyphs (0-9, 10 blank), LBL 11-85 the keys (their KEY? codes, XEQ IND 33),
@ LBL 86-89 + - x /, LBL 90-93 the % of each, LBL 94-96 the cost, the selling price, the margin.
@ Control flow in the C47 STRUCT commands (IF / ELSE / ENDIF, DO / WHILE / ENDDO), indented two spaces
@ per level; tools/build_mh10m.py checks them and numbers them.
@

LBL "MH10M"
@ the user's stack in the local registers: STOS R.00, LASTx in R.08; R.09 the value at the end
LocR 10
STOS R.00
LASTx
STO R.08
XEQ 97                          ; -> :INIT:
@
@ ---- keys: x<>y (42) the end; a key of R85 runs its label (XEQ IND 33); the others ignored ----
DO 01
@   wait for a key: PAUSE 50, KEY? 33 (true: no key yet), as Elements 47
  DO 02
    PAUSE 50
    KEY? 33
  WHILE 02
  ENDDO 02
  RCL 33
  42
  X≠Y?
WHILE 01
@   "/k/" in the keys used R85 (αPOS: -1 when not there)
  "/"
  STO 75
  RCL 33
  αIP 75
  "/"
  x→α 75
  RCL 75
  αPOS 85
  X≥0?
  XEQ 17                        ; -> :KEY:
ENDDO 01
@
@ ---- x<>y: the end: the value in R.09, R20-R91 cleared, GRMOD 0, GRFNT 20, the screen; the user's
@ stack and LASTx back, the value in X ----
RCL 20
STO R.09
20.72
R-CLR
0
GRMOD
20
GRFNT
CLLCD
RCL R.08
STO L
RCLS R.00
RCL R.09
RTN
@ LBL :KEY: the key R33: no indicator of a key (R35), its label, then it is the key before (R34)
LBL 17                          ; :KEY:
0
STO 35
XEQ IND 33
RCL 33
STO 34
RTN
