@ LBL :DIG: the digit X keyed: a new number (LBL :NEWE:) unless one is being keyed; at most 10 digits;
@ N = 10N + d; after the point one decimal more (LBL :DECD:), before it one digit more unless N is 0
LBL 18                          ; :DIG:
STO 75
RCL 30
X≠0?
RTN
RCL 25
X=0?
XEQ 27                          ; -> :NEWE:
10
RCL 27
X≥Y?
RTN
RCL 26
10
×
RCL 75
+
STO 26
RCL 28
X≥0?
GTO 19                          ; -> :DECD:
@ N not 0: one digit more (X≠0? 1: the 1 added, else N = 0 added)
RCL 26
X≠0?
1
STO+ 27
GTO 20                          ; -> :EVAL:
LBL 19                          ; :DECD:
1
STO+ 28
STO+ 27
