@ for one digit, / 10 for each digit more), |X| = IP(|X| R76) / R76; then its decimals R46 and N = the
@ digits as an integer (R45); R20 = N / 10^decimals with the sign of X (x (1 - 2 negative)), also in R86:
@ R45 and R46 are those of R86 (LBL :SHOW: does not cut it again) ----
